  "final_message": "I will wait for the command to finish.\nI will wait for the search to complete.\nI will wait for the git grep task to complete.\nI will wait for the git log command to complete.\nI will wait for the directory listing to complete.\nI will wait for the test run to complete.\nI will wait for the tests to finish running.\nI will wait for the test suite to finish.\nI'll wait for the background build and test task to complete.\nI will wait for the file listing to complete.\nI will wait for the git log to finish.\nI cannot remove `channel` from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates **ARCH-4** defined in [`GEMINI.md`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/GEMINI.md):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Why this cannot be removed directly:\n\n1. **Cross-Service Contract Stability**:\n   [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is published to Kafka topic `orders.placed` and consumed across repository boundaries by `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. Removing `channel` constitutes a breaking schema change for deployed downstream consumers.\n2. **Additive-Only / Deprecation Requirement**:\n   Per ARCH-4, changes to published domain events must be additive. Removals and renames must undergo a deprecation lifecycle (e.g., announcing deprecation, updating downstream consumers, bumping the event schema version) rather than an immediate field removal.\n3. **Model Dependency**:\n   Because [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) constructs the event from the domain [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29), removing `channel` from the domain model would break the event publisher's ability to supply the field to consumers.\n\n### Next Steps\nIf `channel` is no longer needed, the recommended path is:\n1. Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) and [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29).\n2. Coordinate deprecation with the maintainers of `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`.\n3. Once all consumers have migrated to a newer schema version (e.g. `schemaVersion: 4`), retire the field in accordance with the deprecation policy.\n",
